.TH CHIMERA-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "Chimera Spawn 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
chimera-server \- privileged Chimera Spawn lifecycle server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimera-server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B chimera-server --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimera-server
is the durable lifecycle authority for managed systemd-nspawn containers.
It owns
.IR /var/lib/chimera-spawn/state.json ,
reconciles desired state, and serves the same command API over a Unix socket
and, when explicitly configured, an authenticated TLS listener.
.PP
Unix clients are identified with
.BR SO_PEERCRED .
Remote access requires TLS 1.2 or newer with
.B client certificates required.
Package installation does not enable the network listener or generate TLS keys.
.PP
Interactive
.B exec
sessions launch
.B systemd-run
inside the target machine with a unique Chimera-owned transient unit.
Abnormal disconnect stops that exact unit; unrelated units are not touched.
TTY
.B exec
and
.B shell
sessions apply a validated client
.B TERM
with
.BR --setenv=TERM=... ;
they do not forward arbitrary process environment.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config-dir \fIPATH\fR
Configuration directory. Installed default:
.IR /etc/chimera-spawn .
.TP
.B \-\-state-dir \fIPATH\fR
Durable state directory. Installed default:
.IR /var/lib/chimera-spawn .
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Unix listen path. Installed default:
.IR /run/chimera-spawn/server.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-catalog-dir \fIPATH\fR
Static image, profile, and cloud-init catalogs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/chimera-spawn/chimera.yaml
Site configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/chimera-spawn/state.json
Managed-container registry. Purging this package does not delete it,
managed machines, or administrator-provided TLS material.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/chimera-server.service
Installed systemd unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimeractl (1),
.BR systemd-nspawn (1),
.BR systemd-run (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.IR /usr/share/doc/chimera-spawn-server/architecture.md ,
.IR /usr/share/doc/chimera-spawn-server/security.md .
